  "title": "1.1 Outcomes, Events, and Counting",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": "Definition 1.1.1. An outcome is one particular possible result of an experiment. The sample space, usually denoted by $\\Omega$, is the nonempty set consisting of all possible outcomes. An event is a subset of the sample space. For example, if one die is rolled, the event that an even number appears is",
